=Write social captions for a short AI walkthrough video of a real listing. Use only these facts:
Address: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Property Address'] }}
Asking price: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Asking Price'] || 'not given' }}
Bedrooms: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Bedrooms'] || 'not given' }} | Bathrooms: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Bathrooms'] || 'not given' }} | Interior size: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Interior Size'] || 'not given' }}
Key features: {{ ($('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Key Features'] || 'none given').replace(/\n/g, '; ') }}
Rooms shown, in order: {{ $json.rooms.join(', ') }}
Listed by: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Agent and Brokerage'] }}
Listing link: {{ $('When Listing Submitted Trigger').first().json['Listing Link'] || 'none' }}
Tone: {{ $('Set Walkthrough Configurations').first().json.caption_tone }}

Return:
- tiktok_caption: under 300 characters, ending with 3-5 hashtags that include {{ $('Set Walkthrough Configurations').first().json.extra_hashtags }}.
- instagram_caption: under 600 characters, short line breaks, hashtags at the end (include {{ $('Set Walkthrough Configurations').first().json.extra_hashtags }}).
- facebook_caption: under 600 characters, at most 2 hashtags, include the listing link if one is given.
- linkedin_caption: under 700 characters, professional, 0-3 hashtags, include the listing link if one is given.

Fair housing rules (US Fair Housing Act and similar laws): describe the property, never the people who should live there. Never mention or imply race, color, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, familial status, national origin, age or source of income. Do not write phrases like 'perfect for families', 'great for kids', 'adults only', 'ideal for retirees', 'young professionals', 'bachelor pad' or 'exclusive community'. No steering: say nothing about who lives in the area, its safety or crime, school quality, or nearby places of worship. Only state accessibility features if they are in the key features, and state them as facts. No claims beyond the facts given: no invented room sizes, views, upgrades, investment returns, 'won't last' urgency or superlatives like 'best'. Do not write an AI disclosure or a disclaimer; one is added automatically.

